QuickJS for okernel
===================

Upstream: QuickJS 2026-06-04 by Fabrice Bellard and Charlie Gordon
(https://bellard.org/quickjs/, MIT license, see LICENSE). Only the engine
files are vendored: quickjs.c/.h, quickjs-atom.h, quickjs-opcode.h,
cutils.c/.h, list.h, libregexp*, libunicode*, dtoa.c/.h. No quickjs-libc,
no qjs/qjsc.

Local changes (search for "okernel" in the sources):

  quickjs.c   CONFIG_ATOMICS is off when QJS_NO_ATOMICS is defined (no
              threads in the kernel).
  quickjs.c/h JS_EVAL_FLAG_NO_RESOLVE: compile a module without loading its
              imports (JS_ResolveModule() does that later).
  quickjs.c/h JS_FindLoadedModule(), JS_GetModuleRequestCount(),
              JS_GetModuleRequest(): module graph introspection so the host
              can fetch a module graph asynchronously before linking it.
  quickjs.c/h JS_SetDynamicImportHook() + JS_LoadModuleDeferred(): the host
              may park an import() until its module has been fetched.

Kernel build (Makefile QJS_*): compiled hosted-style (builtins on) with
-nostdinc against the freestanding libc in libc/ (headers) + qjs_libc.c
(heap = kmalloc, stdio = serial, clock = RTC + PIT ticks, abort() unwinds
the current page realm via __builtin_longjmp) and the musl libm subset in
libm/ (musl 1.2.5, MIT, see libm/COPYRIGHT.musl; libm/sqrt_x87.c is local).
Doubles use the x87 at 53-bit precision (wjs.c sets the control word on
every entry; libc/float.h reports FLT_EVAL_METHOD 0 accordingly); the
kernel FNSAVEs the FPU per thread on preemptive switches (process.c).

Verification: tests/qjs/build.sh links these exact objects into a
freestanding 32-bit Linux binary (no glibc) and runs QuickJS's own suites
(tests/qjs/suite: language, closures, loops, builtins, BigInt). Host
builds of the web engine (tests/web/build.sh) compile QuickJS against the
system libc instead.
